A||||3||huggy||Horn button order||||5||
Z||000000||huggy||09-22-2000||10:43 AM||||While trying to fix my horn on my 84 se<BR>upon removing the stearing wheel horn cap<BR>three parts flew out at me a spring a thingy<BR>that looks like a nail with a head on it and<BR>a black plastic piece. My question is what order do these parts go into the stearing wheel hole for the horn switch.||||reg||5
Z||000001||HugGRRRFiero||09-22-2000||11:36 AM||||Spring goes in first.  Next, the the nail head lookin thingy goes next (should have a wire attached to it which will connect to the horn button).  If not, you'll need to solder a new one on or find another.  Feed the black plastic thingy over the wire, you should see a notch in the whiteish plastic piece in the column.  Align the tab on the black thingy, press and turn it so the tab is captured by the wishish plastic piece to hold it in.  Hope this helps, sorry about the "thingy" verbage<P>------------------<BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">         <BR>         <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by HugGRRRFiero (edited 09-22-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||huggy||09-22-2000||02:18 PM||||HuGRRRFiero, Where on the naily thing do you solder the wire. Can I use bell wire?. Also where and how is the other end of the wire connected to the horn hub.<p>[This message has been edited by huggy (edited 09-22-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||HugGRRRFiero||09-23-2000||12:04 AM||||Ok, when I wrote the previous post I was thinking of the GT Grant wheel on my car and not the stock one.  The Grant wheel has a wire that replaces the pin with the nail head end.  so please nevermind that post, sorry.<P>I'll start over.<P>I believe you will need to bolt the wheel on first, making sure the hole lines up with the hole in the column for the horn pin.<P>Drop the spring in first.  Next drop the pin in with the flat head going in first against the spring.  Last the black plastic piece goes over the pin and you need to align the tab, push in, and rotate it carefully to hook into the slot in the white plastic piece in the column.  it's really tough to see the groove you'll want to be careful that you don't break that white plastic piece.  Look in the hole with a flashlight if you need to.  The black piece should stay in place and you should be able to push the metal pin sticking out.  See that it moves in and out ok, and that the spring is holding tension.  Pop the center horn cap on the wheel and try the horn.  If you need any more help just let me know.  I appologize about the mis-info, need anything just let me or the forum know.||||reg||1
